  "body": "Full-audit integration fix after restoring the adaptive scheduler.\n\nA local BrowserCapacityUnavailable deferral used `completeRun(... reportQueued=true)`. In the adaptive scheduler, a reported successful completion resets that job type's failure counter. Therefore a job that had already failed could lose its escalating backoff merely because the next due attempt waited for local RAM/CPU capacity without running.\n\nThis adds a dedicated capacity-deferral path that:\n- releases the scheduler claim;\n- retries shortly (current 5s behavior);\n- preserves existing per-job failure counters;\n- does not create a failure or a success event;\n- leaves session and marketplace state untouched.\n\nRegression coverage proves a catalog failure sequence remains 2m -> capacity wait -> 5m on the next real failure.",
  "created_at": "2026-09-18T19:10:50Z",
